          "statement": "Let $d\\ge1$, let $\\mathbb S^d$ be the real vector space of symmetric $d\\times d$ matrices, and set $m=d(d+1)/2$. Use one-based entry labels $A_{ij}:=A(i-1,j-1)$ for $1\\le i,j\\le d$, and likewise for every matrix below. Equip $\\mathbb S^d$ with the Frobenius inner product $\\langle A,B\\rangle_F:=\\sum_{i=1}^{d}\\sum_{j=1}^{d}A_{ij}B_{ij}$ and its induced norm. Define $\\operatorname{svec}:\\mathbb S^d\\to\\mathbb R^m$ by listing $A_{11},\\ldots,A_{dd}$ first, followed by $\\sqrt2 A_{ij}$ for $1\\le i<j\\le d$ in lexicographic order. Then $\\operatorname{svec}$ is a linear bijection and preserves inner products and norms; in particular, $\\|\\operatorname{svec}(A)-\\operatorname{svec}(B)\\|_2=\\|A-B\\|_F$ for all $A,B\\in\\mathbb S^d$."
