          "statement": "Fix positive finite dimensions $d_x,d_h,d_y$, a finite horizon $T\\in\\mathbb N$, a parameter set $\\Theta$, an initial state $h_0\\in\\mathbb R^{d_h}$, and inputs $x_1,\\ldots,x_T\\in\\mathbb R^{d_x}$. A shared-parameter recurrent neural network is specified by a state map $F:\\mathbb R^{d_h}\\times\\mathbb R^{d_x}\\times\\Theta\\to\\mathbb R^{d_h}$ and, optionally, an output map $G:\\mathbb R^{d_h}\\times\\mathbb R^{d_x}\\times\\Theta\\to\\mathbb R^{d_y}$. For a fixed $\\theta\\in\\Theta$, it computes $h_t=F(h_{t-1},x_t;\\theta)$ and, when $G$ is supplied, $y_t=G(h_t,x_t;\\theta)$ for $1\\le t\\le T$, using the same $\\theta$ at every time. Its unrolling is the finite directed acyclic computation graph whose vertices are the input, state, output, and map-evaluation occurrences and whose edges record which values each evaluation uses. The folded schematic may show a feedback edge, while the time-indexed unrolled graph is acyclic.\n\nFor horizon $T=2$, the following TikZ graph shows the dependency edges in the unrolling. The boxes $F_1,F_2$ are two time-indexed occurrences of the same map $F$; the dashed edges indicate that both occurrences receive the identical parameter $\\theta$. The graph omits the optional output map $G$.\n\n\\begin{center}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[>=stealth, every node/.style={draw, rounded corners, inner sep=4pt}]\n  \\node (h0) at (0,0) {$h_0$};\n  \\node (x1) at (0,-1.1) {$x_1$};\n  \\node (f1) at (2,-0.55) {$F_1$};\n  \\node (h1) at (4,-0.55) {$h_1$};\n  \\node (x2) at (4,-1.65) {$x_2$};\n  \\node (f2) at (6,-1.1) {$F_2$};\n  \\node (h2) at (8,-1.1) {$h_2$};\n  \\node (theta) at (4,1) {$\\theta$};\n  \\draw[->] (h0) -- (f1);\n  \\draw[->] (x1) -- (f1);\n  \\draw[->] (f1) -- (h1);\n  \\draw[->] (h1) -- (f2);\n  \\draw[->] (x2) -- (f2);\n  \\draw[->] (f2) -- (h2);\n  \\draw[->, dashed] (theta) -- (f1);\n  \\draw[->, dashed] (theta) -- (f2);\n\\end{tikzpicture}\n\\end{center}",
