        {
          "id": "alg-cauchy-matvec-at-roots-of-unity",
          "kind": "algorithm",
          "title": "Exact Cauchy matrix-vector product on a radix-two root grid",
          "statement": "Input an integer $M=2^q$ with $q\\ge0$, a primitive $M$th root of unity $\\omega$, a finite list of poles $\\mu_1,\\ldots,\\mu_n\\in\\mathbb C$, and weights $a_1,\\ldots,a_n\\in\\mathbb C$. The required output is $y_k=\\sum_{j=1}^n a_j/(\\omega^k-\\mu_j)$ for $0\\le k<M$, provided no denominator is zero. If $n=0$, return the zero vector.\n\nHere a primitive $M$th root means $\\omega^M=1$ and $\\omega^k\\ne1$ for $1\\le k<M$. For $n\\ge1$, form a balanced binary tree on the pole indices, splitting each consecutive index interval into two intervals whose sizes differ by at most one. At a leaf containing index $j$, store polynomials $D_j(z)=z-\\mu_j$ and $P_j(z)=a_j$. At an internal node with disjoint child index sets $I_1,I_2$, store\n$$ D_I(z)=D_{I_1}(z)D_{I_2}(z),\\qquad P_I(z)=P_{I_1}(z)D_{I_2}(z)+D_{I_1}(z)P_{I_2}(z). $$\nAt the root, fold the coefficients of each polynomial modulo $z^M-1$: the coefficient at degree $r$ is replaced by the sum of coefficients at degrees congruent to $r$ modulo $M$. Let $\\omega_0=e^{-2\\pi i/M}$, which equals $1$ when $M=1$. Apply the radix-two DFT procedure to each folded coefficient vector to evaluate $P_I$ and $D_I$ at $\\omega_0^j$, $0\\le j<M$. If $M>1$, find the unique odd integer $s\\in\\{1,3,\\ldots,M-1\\}$ with $\\omega=\\omega_0^s$ by generating and comparing the $M$ powers of $\\omega_0$, then place the value at index $sk\\bmod M$ at output index $k$; this is the supplied root order because $\\omega^k=\\omega_0^{sk}$. For $M=1$, the only root is $1$ and no reindexing is needed. This root search and reindexing use $O(M)$ operations. If some reindexed $D_I(\\omega^k)=0$, return status `collision`; otherwise return $y_k=P_I(\\omega^k)/D_I(\\omega^k)$.",
          "deps": [
            "alg-radix-two-fft"
          ],
          "dependency_level": 1,
          "sources": {
            "references": [
