        {
          "id": "thm-hippo-leg-matrices-have-low-rank-structure",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "HiPPO LegS, LegT, and LagT generators have normal-plus-low-rank form",
          "statement": "Index rows and columns by $0,\\ldots,N-1$. Define the real LegS coefficient matrix $G^S$ by $G^S_{nk}=-\\sqrt{(2n+1)(2k+1)}$ when $n>k$, $G^S_{nn}=-(n+1)$, and $G^S_{nk}=0$ when $n<k$. In the LegS coefficient ODE for $t>0$ this matrix is multiplied by the time-dependent scalar $1/t$; the matrix assertion below does not make that ODE time-invariant. For $\\theta>0$, define the LegT state generator by $G^T_{nk}=-(2n+1)(-1)^{n-k}/\\theta$ when $n\\ge k$ and $G^T_{nk}=-(2n+1)/\\theta$ when $n<k$. Define the original HiPPO LagT state generator by $G^L_{nk}=-1$ when $n\\ge k$ and $G^L_{nk}=0$ when $n<k$. Here $X^*$ is conjugate transpose, a complex matrix $H$ is normal when $H^*H=HH^*$, and a square matrix $V$ is unitary when $V^*V=VV^*=I$. For LegS and LagT use the identity similarity; for LegT use the invertible diagonal similarity $S_0=\\operatorname{diag}(\\sqrt{2n+1})_{n=0}^{N-1}\\operatorname{diag}((-1)^n)_{n=0}^{N-1}$. Each transformed matrix is a difference $H-UV^*$ with $H$ normal and $\\operatorname{rank}(UV^*)\\le1$ for LegS and LagT and $\\operatorname{rank}(UV^*)\\le2$ for LegT. Consequently the equivalent finite-dimensional complex state-space matrix has a normal-plus-low-rank representation, and a unitary change of state coordinates gives diagonal-plus-low-rank form. Under any state change $x=S\\widetilde x$, the input and output vectors change to $S^{-1}B$ and $S^*C$, respectively.",
          "deps": [
