        {
          "id": "thm-cauchy-matvec-at-roots-of-unity-exact-cost",
          "kind": "theorem",
          "title": "Exact roots-of-unity Cauchy matvec has quasi-linear arithmetic cost",
          "statement": "Let $n\\ge1$, $M=2^q\\ge1$, $\\omega$ be a primitive $M$th root of unity, and let $\\mu_1,\\ldots,\\mu_n\\in\\mathbb C$ and $a_1,\\ldots,a_n\\in\\mathbb C$ satisfy $\\mu_j\\ne\\omega^k$ for every $j$ and $0\\le k<M$. Then the Cauchy matrix-vector product $y_k=\\sum_{j=1}^{n}a_j/(\\omega^k-\\mu_j)$, $0\\le k<M$, is computed exactly by the balanced product-tree procedure using $O((n+M)\\log^2(2+n+M))$ complex arithmetic operations and $O(n+M)$ space. Repeated poles are allowed.",
