          "kind": "algorithm",
          "title": "Radix-two discrete Fourier transform",
          "statement": "For a nonnegative integer $q$, let $M=2^q$, set $\\omega=1$ when $M=1$ and $\\omega=e^{-2\\pi i/M}$ when $M>1$, and let $a=(a_0,\\ldots,a_{M-1})\\in\\mathbb C^M$. The forward discrete Fourier transform (DFT) is the vector $\\widehat a\\in\\mathbb C^M$ with $\\widehat a_k=\\sum_{j=0}^{M-1}a_j\\omega^{jk}$. The radix-two procedure returns this vector by the following exact recursion. If $M=1$, return $(a_0)$. If $M>1$, recursively compute the length-$M/2$ DFTs $E$ and $O$ of $(a_0,a_2,\\ldots,a_{M-2})$ and $(a_1,a_3,\\ldots,a_{M-1})$, using the primitive root $\\omega^2$. For $0\\le k<M/2$, return $\\widehat a_k=E_k+\\omega^k O_k$ and $\\widehat a_{k+M/2}=E_k-\\omega^kO_k$. The inverse transform is obtained by running the same procedure with $\\overline\\omega$ and dividing every output by $M$.",
