          "id": "def-lstm-cell",
          "kind": "definition",
          "title": "Standard LSTM cell",
          "statement": "Fix positive finite dimensions $d_x,d_h$, inputs $x_t\\in\\mathbb R^{d_x}$, hidden states $h_t\\in\\mathbb R^{d_h}$, cell states $c_t\\in\\mathbb R^{d_h}$, and initial values $h_0,c_0$. A standard long short-term memory (LSTM) cell without peephole connections or projection has shared matrices $W_i,W_f,W_o,W_c\\in\\mathbb R^{d_h\\times d_x}$, $U_i,U_f,U_o,U_c\\in\\mathbb R^{d_h\\times d_h}$, and biases $b_i,b_f,b_o,b_c\\in\\mathbb R^{d_h}$. Apply $\\sigma(s)=(1+e^{-s})^{-1}$ and $\\tanh(s)=(e^s-e^{-s})/(e^s+e^{-s})$ coordinatewise. At each time $t\\ge1$, set\n\n$$ i_t=\\sigma(W_i x_t+U_i h_{t-1}+b_i),\\qquad f_t=\\sigma(W_f x_t+U_f h_{t-1}+b_f),\\qquad o_t=\\sigma(W_o x_t+U_o h_{t-1}+b_o), $$\n\n$$ g_t=\\tanh(W_c x_t+U_c h_{t-1}+b_c),\\qquad c_t=f_t\\odot c_{t-1}+i_t\\odot g_t,\\qquad h_t=o_t\\odot\\tanh(c_t), $$\n\nwhere $\\odot$ is coordinatewise multiplication. The same matrices and biases are reused at every time step. The vectors $i_t,f_t,o_t$ are the input, forget, and output gates, and $g_t$ is the candidate state update.",
