          "title": "A fixed-rank DPLR bilinear recurrent step has linear arithmetic cost",
          "statement": "Let $N,r\\ge1$, let $A=\\Lambda-PQ^*$ with diagonal $\\Lambda\\in\\mathbb C^{N\\times N}$ and $P,Q\\in\\mathbb C^{N\\times r}$, where $^*$ denotes conjugate transpose, let $B,C\\in\\mathbb C^N$, and let $\\Delta>0$. If $G=I-\\Delta A/2$ is invertible, then one bilinear recurrent update and its scalar output can be computed using $O(N(r+1)^2+(r+1)^3)$ exact complex arithmetic operations and $O(N(r+1)+(r+1)^2)$ working space. For fixed $r$, this is $O(N)$ operations and $O(N)$ space. When the diagonal base $I-\\Delta\\Lambda/2$ is invertible, the required $r\\times r$ Woodbury correction is invertible. When that diagonal base is singular but $G$ is invertible, the bordered correction in the recurrent algorithm is invertible and has size at most $2r$.",
